TIP:  Pete Seger and Lee Hays wrote this old folk/protest song way back in 1949 and, politics aside, it's been covered by many artists since then including Peter, Paul, and Mary.  But I like Trini Lopez's jumpy version from 1963. 

TIP:  There's a driving chord progression that starts with the intro and keeps going throughout the entire song.  Note that the "ooh ohhs" end in (F) and immediately go to the (G) in the verse. 


